WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:06.530
Once upon a time, there was a traveler crouching in pain at the roadside.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:12.340
A man, who happened to be walking by, sat next to the traveler before he could ask for help.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:21.810
The man lectured at length about having a healthy lifestyle in order to avoid sickness.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:27.350
Satisfied with his speech, the man stood up and left.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:32.920
The man's name is the United Mankind.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:43.700
Next, a very beautiful woman approached the traveler with an inquisitive look.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:50.340
The traveler said, "Well, don't just stand there, help me."

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:57.950
The woman replied, "Do you want me to help you?"

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:08.290
She then discussed at length the situation with the traveler until she fully understood the problem. And she nodded and left.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:17.400
Shortly after, the woman brought all the doctors, nurses, and staff of the closest hospital with her.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.370
The woman's name is the Humankind Empire Abh.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:29.280
A political allegory from Planet Midgrat

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:04.680
Raïchacarh Üacr Sauder Sfagnomr

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:04.680
Sfagnomr Gateway Battle

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.210
What's this?!

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.090
99.97% probability that it's the enemy fleet.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.590
I already know that!

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.590
We made a show of force to scare them away.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.630
Yes...

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.590
...perhaps more than necessary.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.430
The enemy has no chance of winning, right?

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.510
That's right.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.560
Any rational commander would come to that conclusion.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.810
Then why?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.900
Why do they still remain in this area?!

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:45.200
99.97% possibility?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.530
What's the remaining 0.03%?

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:51.490
Deceptive information caused by failure of sensory devices...

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.790
...or an unknown natural phenomenon, or unidentified intelligent beings...

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.460
All right. That's enough.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.960
I had the impression that you wanted a battle.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.880
I prefer not to fight with any doubts in my mind.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.010
What do you make of their position?

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.410
Firstly...

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.410
...there is the possibility the enemy thinks it can win.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.360
Win?

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.020
Against all this military power?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.280
The enemy ships may be capable of far more than we estimate.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.280
You think we've misunderstood their technical ability?

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.740
What do you expect...

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.330
...from the division in charge of feeding cats?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.460
Oh, that's right!

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.330
The Information Bureau can only do jobs like feeding cats.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.840
Actually...

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.920
...I rate the Information Bureau somewhat higher than you do.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.550
It's not likely that the enemy is capable of more than we expect.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.220
If the enemy thinks that it can win...

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.230
...perhaps there's a problem with their leader's state of mind.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.400
There's no glory in fighting a clown.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.360
As to the second possibility...

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.070
...remember that their main force is the United Mankind.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.280
What are you getting at?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.280
Its military command is known for handing out inflexible orders.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.160
Like an order to defend Sufugnoff using minimal resources.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.790
If that was the order...

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:14.330
Concentrating all of their forces in this area would be the rational move.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:15.790
That's it!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.800
That's got to be it!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:23.010
Right this moment, my doubts have vanished, like stardust entering the atmosphere...

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.300
...wiping away all misgivings from my heart...

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.510
I'm confident of our victory!

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.720
I thank you so much, Major Kahyul!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.270
I'm honored.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.850
Now that that's clear, there's no reason to hesitate!

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.360
Prepare for encirclement!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:37.610
That wouldn't be wise.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.610
Why not?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.700
We're too close to the enemy.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.030
If we spread out to encircle them from this distance...

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.490
...we may isolate parts of our fleet, making them vulnerable.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:51.620
Although we'd still win, we would incur great losses.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.830
Shuril?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.460
He's right.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.210
In that case, we'll meet them head on..

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.170
I think that would be the better strategy.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:09.010
Inspector, the Condrin group says they're done for now...

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.810
...and wants to know where to go next.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.640
I'll check with the reserves.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.850
Standby until we figure out our next move.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.480
Roger.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.280
<i>Inspector, I'm with</i> <i>Chief Ramashdi.</i>

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.280
<i>We're stuck at an occupation</i> <i>army road block.</i>

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.950
Not again...

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.490
This is the tenth time!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.750
Why can't they be more flexible?!

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.670
Here, it's for you again.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.630
I'll speak with the officer in charge from our army.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.130
Yes.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.630
Three more hotels...

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:48.720
Where are you, young Abh lady?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.180
...thank you very much.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:55.640
Cloge  Dac  Limzairh

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.980
Limzairh Inn

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.360
I'll put yours here.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:06:59.940
Okay.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.610
<i>The purpose was to</i> <i>investigate deep space.</i>

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.700
<i>Rather than using</i> <i>genuine machines...</i>

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.570
<i>...they thought organic machines</i> <i>would be more suitable.</i>

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.700
<i>And that's what the Abh are.</i>

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.410
<i>In other words,</i> <i>Abh are not human.</i>

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.290
<i>They are nothing more</i> <i>than organic machines.</i>

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.630
I should've added more salt.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>I call out to all free humans.</i>

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.720
<i>We must put the Abh</i> <i>back where they belong.</i>

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.930
<i>As living machines</i> <i>made to serve humanity!</i>

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:30.550
<i>It would also...</i>

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.140
They're full of lies!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.640
What she said is no lie.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:40.900
It's true that our ancestors were created as living machines.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.650
Did you not know that?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.690
I had no idea.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.490
Not surprising.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:49.030
The Abh will never talk about it...

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.620
...and you won't find it written anywhere.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.200
It's only told within the family, from generation to generation.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.210
This is very salty.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.370
Oh, sorry.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.750
I'll make it more to your liking next time.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.880
Our ancestors...

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.710
...were sent on an expedition by their mother fortress...

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.470
...to search the depths of space.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.680
During that journey...

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.350
...they discovered a new speed portal...

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.850
...that we now know as Saudec Loeza.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.520
After that, they decided to break from the mother fortress...

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.690
...and live independently in outer space.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.100
I see.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.060
Yes.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:28.240
And in order to fend off forces sent by the space fortress...

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.950
...they developed their own military and weapons...

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:31.990
But...

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:36.240
...the fortress didn't have the resources to send a force, right?

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.790
That's right.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.830
But we still ended up destroying it.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:43.420
Why?

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.630
I asked my father the same question.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.590
My father said that our ancestors were...

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.840
...afraid of the space fortress.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.850
They were almost crushed by their own mounting fear.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:02.440
The shadow of the space fortress kept looming so large and powerful over them.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.310
I don't get it.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.690
I don't get it either.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:11.910
My father taught me that every Abh must carry the guilt and mission on one's shoulders.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:13.070
And I believe he's right.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:16.830
The guilt of destroying the space fortress.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.870
And the mission?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.790
To protect and convey the culture of the mother fortress.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.460
Even though they hated it?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.540
It's not hatred.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:27.750
It's love.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.590
That's what our ancestors said...

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.180
...as they watched the debris scatter in space.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.930
I'm going to bed.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.440
Okay.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:44.690
Jinto?

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:45.440
Yeah?

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.610
Do you regret becoming an Abh?

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.690
Why should I regret it?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.700
I'm already an Abh.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.490
You taught me that yourself.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.240
Good night!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.410
Good night.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.670
There are some things I still don't understand.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:06.710
In fact...

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.210
...my mind's full of things I don't understand.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:10.760
Yet...

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:16.760
...I've accepted my destiny as an Abh.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.270
Why, this is...!

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:25.480
What is it?

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.520
The military police has made its move.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.520
Well, how delightful.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.280
So I guess they no longer need us.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.150
No.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:36.240
We must inform HQ as soon as we find out where they are...

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.950
...and keep an eye on them.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.330
What'd you say?

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.410
We can't go in and arrest them?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:43.830
No.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.250
The military police will be making the arrest.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.920
That's ridiculous!

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.630
We're told to do all the work...

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.590
...yet we can only watch as they move in on the offenders?

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.090
There's a strong possibility that the Abh we're after...

00:10:55.090 --> 00:11:00.640
...were on that shuttle entering from Plane Space.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.850
So what?

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.600
It's also likely that they came from the enemy ship...

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.690
...that our forces destroyed in Plane Space.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.530
If that's the case, they could have some crucial information.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.240
Such as?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.910
I have no idea.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.280
And I couldn't tell you if I did.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.750
Likely not.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.290
So, those Abh are even more valuable than we thought..

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.580
If we find them...

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.800
...I'm sure your department would look at it favorably.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.800
I think I'm figuring all this out.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.930
You don't want the local police to be the heroes.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.800
No.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.930
They don't want me to be the hero.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.520
Why not?

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:46.100
You're certainly one of the selected few...

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.480
...becoming a lieutenant at such a young age.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.150
Young?

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:50.980
Me?

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.400
Inspector, how old do you think I am?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.460
Don't move, or I'll shoot.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:09.420
Who are you?!

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.460
Don't we look like police officers?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.300
Police...!

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.680
There's a girl staying with you, isn't there?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.680
An Abh girl.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:23.050
No.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.100
I think you have the wrong room.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.810
Hey, check the bedroom.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:29.690
Stop!

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:38.990
That was brave. Very brave.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.200
But if you move one more time, I swear I'll shoot!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.200
Did you come to arrest us?

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.370
That's what I understand.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.370
Understand?

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.540
Shut up! I'll explain later!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.000
Hey.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.210
Let go, you little punk!

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:01.510
Damn!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.220
Quite a sense of loyalty you have.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.980
We'd rather have you walk on your own feet...

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.650
...but it's not a must.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.690
Have you ever been shot before?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:20.610
What are you waiting for?

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.820
Check the room!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.760
An Abh!

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.600
They really exist.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.100
Drop your weapon, Abh.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.400
Don't you care what happens to him?

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.190
Even a tranquilizer gun will kill him from this distance.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:01.240
I suggest you think it over.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.110
Th-Think it over?!

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:05.070
Should you kill him, you will all die here.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.120
I won't allow any of you to leave this room alive.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.080
Keep in mind that I'm in an extremely bad mood.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.040
Because we woke you up from your sleep?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.100
Don't shoot! I haven't done anything.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.610
It's a good thing that you thought it over.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.400
Wh-What the-

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:49.950
Why, you're...

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.500
How clumsy can you guys be?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.080
So, you're not a chambermaid.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.710
No.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.420
I'm their leader, Marca.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.340
I'm a crew member on the anti-imperial warship, Clasebyr.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:14.100
Is it just me who thinks this is starting to look like an...

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.810
...execution?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.770
Just call me Undertaker.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.110
I have my own name, but my friends call me that.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.780
I'm Min.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:29.530
My parents gave me a different name, but I don't like it.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.120
Just call me Min.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:32.990
I'm Bill.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.620
Everyone knows the name Bill Tobashja in this city.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.330
Daswani.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.590
I want you to listen to what we have to say.

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:43.590
It'll benefit you as well.

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.510
I wonder about that.

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:48.380
"Anti-imperial" suggests you don't like Abh.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.760
I've got nothing against the Abh.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.720
It's just that we're seeking independence.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.890
We're seeking the right to reject the imperial system...

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.860
...and claim trading and space exploration rights of our own.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.610
There's no way...

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.320
...the Empire would allow that.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.360
That's why we're fighting.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.870
Fighting? Against the Empire?

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.700
Who did you think we were fighting?

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.540
Well, so, how's that going to benefit us?

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.210
We want you to be our hostages.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.590
Jinto, let's go.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:23.630
You're right.

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.170
Wait!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.630
At this rate, you won't get away from them.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:30.930
We can keep you out of sight...

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.510
...until the Abh return.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.100
That would help a great deal.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:37.430
But why do you need hostages?

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.640
To use in our negotiations.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.650
I'll do the talking!

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:43.940
But, yes. He's right.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.730
We want to negotiate with the Empire in exchange...

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.530
...for the young lady there.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:49.860
That's impossible.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.530
That's fine.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.660
All right. Under these conditions.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.700
Hostages giving us conditions?

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:58.620
Go ahead.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.370
We're not handing you our weapons.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.080
Who ever heard of armed hostages?!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.670
Would you be quiet, already?!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:05.670
And...

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.800
...the two of us must always be together.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.550
I accept.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.640
Okay, let's get ready.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.560
Go and get changed.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:17.140
Stop treating me like a child.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.150
They seem pretty ordinary.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:25.690
Are you sure she's nobility, with her attendant?

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.690
They're acting! And they're good.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:30.150
But...

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:34.160
...you're basing your actions on the assumption that the Empire will recapture this place, aren't you?

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:36.700
What if the Empire doesn't return here?

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.000
You think the Abh would give up and walk away from defeat?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:44.170
That's the craziest thing I've heard all year.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.210
The Undertaker's right.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.960
Rokeil, 120 units from the designated location.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.340
Kitiil, all vessels have come about.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.300
Wakapeil, all vessels anchored, on standby.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.640
Byuuldef, procession aligned.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.550
Futuune, maintaining route 027.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.850
Bask Gumlyuf, confirming mutual details within fleet.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:59.310
Enemy space-time separation.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.890
There's a 99.96% probability...

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.190
Skip the percentages!

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.440
...that it's an enemy mine cluster.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.570
I already know that.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.940
It's begun.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.650
Yes.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.280
Commence defensive mine attack!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.500
Contact with space-time bubbles at direction 305.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.340
Distance 65.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:28.880
Contact range increasing.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.090
Deploying mines 1 and 2.

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:31.970
Space-time particles confirmed. Commence progress in unison.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.470
Probability of destroying enemy mine, 83%.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.890
Probability of mine convergence in space-time, 98.6%.

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:40.220
Enemy mine defensive line cluster, at 58 units and closing.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.860
Unit 1, space-time convergence.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.400
Unit 2, space-time convergence.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.900
Unit 3, space-time convergence.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.360
Unit 4, space-time convergence.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.240
Distance to enemy, 142 units.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:58.370
Enemy front line is within our firing range.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:18:59.830
Good.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.410
Reprogram the mine targets to attack the front line.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.420
Reprogramming mine targets.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.170
Target enemy front line.

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.330
lnitial input completed.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.720
Unit 3 has destroyed Alhej.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:18.960
Remaining enemy mines have reached our front line.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.220
Distance to enemy, 100 units.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.680
Okay, now for our next step.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.690
We'll throw Futuune at them.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.020
Transmission from HQ.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.190
Read me the text.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:33.820
Yes.

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.570
Trample them. That's it.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.030
Well...

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:42.200
...this is my first mission with Admiral Trife...

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.040
...but I can see that his orders are nice and concise.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:51.170
Units 1 through 6, generate space-time bubbles of respective units and prepare to mobilize.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.420
Each squadron is to form a horizontal line...

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.630
...and proceed to the front of our fleet.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:56.760
Aye-aye.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.470
Main fleet, remain anchored.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:03.060
Send orders for Number 3 mass formation.

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.430
Unit 4 has fallen behind.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:06.640
I hate laggards.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.270
Very well, I'm sure they'll catch up.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.520
We'll attack with just the other 5 units.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:13.980
But...

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.240
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:20.120
Advise each captain...

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:23.030
...to be completely mobile, and on course 310.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.000
The signal, the continuous message "Follow me".

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.880
Approaching enemy space-time bubbles!

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.010
What in the world?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.390
Th-There's a real battle going on.

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.020
But look at her.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:53.400
Your Excellency.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.190
The enemy is focusing their mine attack on Futuune.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.450
Shouldn't we counter with our defensive mines?

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.490
Where were you posted before you came here, I wonder?

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.740
I was senior staff on the Number 184 attack fleet.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.160
Really?

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.210
I can see why you wouldn't know then.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.040
Listen...

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:16.880
...patrol ships aren't equipped with a single defensive mine.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:19.090
The few mines loaded on a patrol ship...

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.550
...must be used for attacking other vessels.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:22.970
Make sure you remember that.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:24.390
But still...

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.760
There's no arguing this.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:30.890
A patrol ship mustn't start panicking at this level of attack.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:34.230
Besides, we are Futuune.

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:41.070
Transmission from Unit 1, patrol ship Kyul Bulsh.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.600
"Serious damage incurred."

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.910
"Electromagnetic guns and forward cannons inoperative."

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:47.910
"Retreating to the rear."

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.710
Enemy front line is taking action to evade us.

00:21:58.510 --> 00:21:59.710
Shall we go after them?

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.010
Are you a fool?

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:04.300
Or are you just acting like one?

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.760
I'm terribly sorry!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:09.560
I'm asking you a question.

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:10.600
Which is it?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:14.560
Well, I was just acting like a fool.

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:17.570
And why would you do that?

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.730
That's because...

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:23.990
Were you checking whether or not your superior was a fool?

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:25.870
No, never...

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:27.080
Then why did you?

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:28.950
I'm terribly sorry!

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:30.830
It's exactly as you guessed.

00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:34.540
I'll forgive you this one time.

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:36.630
But make sure you never do it again.

00:22:37.130 --> 00:22:40.130
I'll tease you unmercifully next time.

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:41.510
I'll remember that.

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:44.010
Maintain this course.

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:48.510
Our destination is the line of battle.

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:54.190
Leave the small fish like escort vessels for the fleets behind us.

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:57.190
The Undertaker was right.

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:01.690
The Abh had no intention of walking away from this fight.

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:35.950
We should see the enemy's front line fleet any time now.

00:24:35.950 --> 00:24:39.170
Unless we start getting aggressive...

00:24:39.170 --> 00:24:41.080
...Futuune will walk off with the best stuff!

00:24:41.670 --> 00:24:42.250
Hurry!

00:24:44.090 --> 00:24:45.090
It's a dead end.

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:50.720
We are Futuune, the Goddess of Dance.

00:24:50.720 --> 00:24:53.510
Show them what great dancers we are.

00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:59.850
Next episode

00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:59.850
Lady of Chaos

00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:59.850
Logh Labyrena
